// Transform rule: collapse runs of spaces in a value.
//
// BUGGY on purpose: String.replace returns a new string, and the result is thrown away,
// so the loop never ends when the value has a double space. The tester stops it with a timeout.
// Fix: value = value.replace("  ", " ");  (or value.replaceAll("\\s+", " ")).

if (value == null) return null;
while (value.contains("  ")) {
    value.replace("  ", " ");
}
return value.trim();
